WASTEPAY - CORE PWA SCREENS


1. PURPOSE

The WastePay Progressive Web Application exists to provide mobile-first operational interfaces for depot staff, collection drivers, and future operational roles while maintaining offline capabilities, accessibility standards, and enterprise-grade field usability.



--------------------------------------------------


2. UNIVERSAL PWA ARCHITECTURE

All users access:

app.wastepay.org


The system automatically detects user roles and loads the appropriate operational experience.

Supported experiences include:

- Depot Agent Dashboard
- Depot Manager Dashboard
- Pickup Driver Dashboard

Future support includes:

- Collector Dashboard
- WastePay Super Administrator Dashboard



--------------------------------------------------


3. MOBILE-FIRST DESIGN PRINCIPLES

The PWA is optimized for:

- Outdoor usage.
- Bright daylight visibility.
- One-handed operation.
- Field operations.
- Low bandwidth environments.

Design requirements include:

- High contrast interfaces.
- Large typography.
- Large touch targets.
- Premium mobile interactions.
- Responsive layouts.



--------------------------------------------------


4. ACCESSIBILITY STANDARDS

Minimum requirements:

- 48px touch targets.
- High contrast UI.
- Large button components.
- Large form controls.
- Glove-friendly interactions.

Business Rule:

All operational actions must be easily accessible on mobile devices.



--------------------------------------------------


5. UNIVERSAL PWA HEADER

The header includes:

- WastePay logo.
- User information.
- Current shift status.
- Network status.
- GPS status.
- Notification indicator.

Network indicators include:

- ONLINE
- OFFLINE STORAGE ACTIVE



--------------------------------------------------


6. OFFLINE-FIRST CAPABILITIES

The PWA supports:

- Collector check-in.
- Barcode scanning.
- Weight entry.
- Photo capture.
- Pickup completion.
- GPS collection.

Business Rule:

Operational data must be safely stored locally when connectivity is unavailable.



--------------------------------------------------


7. OFFLINE SYNCHRONIZATION WORKFLOW

Data synchronization process:

LOCAL STORAGE

↓

SECURE SYNCHRONIZATION

↓

SUPABASE DATABASE

↓

SYNC COMPLETE



